## Implementation

- `apps/storytime/app/[locale]/st/[level]/[week]/decodable.tsx` (new): the client decodable part.
  The sounds page shows the element, its graphemes, and its sound; a tap plays the bank clip. A page
  word asks `blendPlanForWord` for its plan. A blend word plays its graphemes from the bank in
  reading order, then the whole word from the book recording. A tricky word and a sound-book word
  play whole. The page turner and the tricky-word list stay local. No phone voice (rule 10.5).
- `apps/storytime/lib/phoneme-bank.ts` (new): the 45 G3 clips with the `grapheme` and `file` of each
  one, plus the labeled count `phoneme_clips=45`.
- `apps/storytime/lib/blend.ts`: F28. The longest-grapheme maximum uses a loop, not a spread, so a
  200,000-entry list returns without `RangeError`. A capital word takes the lower-case plan.
- `apps/storytime/app/[locale]/st/[level]/[week]/reader.tsx`: re-exports the decodable part from the
  client reader path.
- `apps/storytime/app/[locale]/st/[level]/[week]/page.tsx`: renders the decodable part for
  `part === "decodable"`. The task 3.1a media gate, the task 3.2 tiles, and the task 3.3 read-along
  reader are unchanged.

